From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homescoop <homescoop@ai-ecoverse.invalid>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:35:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wasi: the filesystem as unix

On WASI uv takes its unix paths: bin/, symlinks (std::os::wasi::fs::
symlink_path), the cache's archive symlinks and the runtime cfg!(unix)
choices. WASI has no permission bits, file locks or descriptor dup:
- which: any regular file on PATH is a candidate;
- file locks are granted and released without a lock;
- atomic writes reopen the temporary file and carry no mode over;
- scripts are made executable with slicc's kernel slicc_fs.fd_chmod,
  which wasix-sysroot's libc uses too (ENOSYS without it: ignored).
